WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.382
Daga and the One-Year Wish. A Philippines story about a roof mouse, a hidden tooth, and a wish that refused to hurry.

00:00:10.382 --> 00:00:17.764
Every December, Lola's house filled with parol stars, strings, and cousins.

00:00:17.764 --> 00:00:27.570
The older cousins reached the eave. Maya pointed out their mistakes. This was also important work.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:37.596
"I can tie the high hook." Maya rose until her tsinelas gave up. Lola caught the string.

00:00:37.596 --> 00:00:48.773
"Next year. It needs patient hands." Maya inspected hers. They were available now.

00:00:48.773 --> 00:01:01.387
At merienda, Maya's loose tooth wobbled against warm bread. All week it had leaned left, then right. Now it seemed ready to announce something.

00:01:01.387 --> 00:01:15.345
Maya bit down. Click. A tiny white tooth sat in her palm while every cousin leaned closer. It looked too small to have caused so much drama.

00:01:15.345 --> 00:01:30.555
Lola rinsed the tooth. "When I was small, we asked Daga, the roof mouse, to hide it. We did not give a tooth only to the night. We gave it time."

00:01:30.555 --> 00:01:36.977
"If we found it after one year, we could make another wish."

00:01:36.977 --> 00:01:47.794
Maya counted twelve months and far too many mornings. Lola smiled. "That gives the wish room to grow."

00:01:47.794 --> 00:02:02.672
Maya drew herself tying the high hook, very tall and very sure. Underneath she wrote, "I wish to be big enough now," then folded the page small.

00:02:02.672 --> 00:02:10.462
Lola opened the screen. Maya tossed the tooth and folded wish onto the low awning.

00:02:10.462 --> 00:02:19.671
"Now we wait," said Lola. Maya immediately wondered how to wait faster.

00:02:19.671 --> 00:02:28.421
Whiskers crossed the awning. A folded ear, silver feet, and a tail vanished with the bundle.

00:02:28.421 --> 00:02:39.630
Three pawprints glowed. "Daga," said Lola, closing the window. "No peeking."

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:50.444
At sunrise, Maya checked the awning, windowsill, and pencil box. Everyone knew mysterious mice liked office supplies.

00:02:50.444 --> 00:02:56.242
She found only shavings and the strong feeling of being laughed at.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:03:04.512
In the drawer, a dusty shadow curled like a question. One silver pawprint crossed it.

00:03:04.512 --> 00:03:11.846
The shadow skittered back. Daga was hiding the wish, not forgetting it.

00:03:11.846 --> 00:03:25.019
Maya flipped eleven calendar pages. "There. One year." The calendar hung crooked on its nail, thoroughly unconvinced.

00:03:25.019 --> 00:03:34.873
A warm glow brushed the window. Tanda touched the silver pawprint, and a path stopped at one closed moon-square.

00:03:34.873 --> 00:03:43.103
"I can see the path," she said. "I cannot shorten it."

00:03:43.103 --> 00:03:51.325
Daga stood on the pencil box wearing a calendar-paper kerchief, one ear folded like a page corner.

00:03:51.325 --> 00:03:58.995
The mouse studied Maya, Tanda, and the calendar, then vanished into silver tracks.

00:03:58.995 --> 00:04:10.553
Daga's tracks drew a silver path: window, drawer, calendar, roofline, moon. The house had been keeping the way all along.

00:04:10.553 --> 00:04:25.063
Twelve paper doors appeared. Eleven showed rain, school shoes, new pencils, and thin moons. Soft light waited behind the twelfth. It would not open.

00:04:25.063 --> 00:04:35.664
"What if waiting means it forgets me?" Maya asked. Daga's tiny voice came from above the calendar.

00:04:35.664 --> 00:04:42.906
"Waiting is not forgetting." Maya let her hands rest in her lap.

00:04:42.906 --> 00:04:50.456
"All right," Maya said. "Hide it where one year can find it."

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:57.670
The calendar straightened, the drawer sighed, and Daga's tracks disappeared near the eave.

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:07.980
Under the eave, Daga tucked the bundle into a patient splinter of wood: the exact place Maya would forget until she was ready to remember.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:11.354
The splinter closed.

00:05:11.354 --> 00:05:25.240
Rain, school shoes, missing pencils, new words, and one grown-up tooth passed by. Maya checked the calendar less often. The calendar did not brag.

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:41.797
One afternoon, the pencil box wiggled. Maya reached for the lid, then stopped. "I know," she said. Inside, something tiny pretended not to be pleased.

00:05:41.797 --> 00:05:47.715
Maya's cousin Nina arrived with a loose tooth and a worried face.

00:05:47.715 --> 00:05:58.389
"It's easy," Maya almost said. Instead she sat beside Nina. "It feels weird at first."

00:05:58.389 --> 00:06:07.643
When the parol box returned, Maya was taller. More importantly, she could hold the string without yanking.

00:06:07.643 --> 00:06:15.985
The high hook looked less like a prize and more like trusted work. One year had passed.

00:06:15.985 --> 00:06:28.911
That night, Maya did not run to the window. She washed her hands, found her old drawing, and waited until the fan, roof, and calendar all sounded ready.

00:06:28.911 --> 00:06:38.957
The patient splinter lifted like a tiny door. The tooth bundle waited inside, smaller and brighter than Maya remembered.

00:06:38.957 --> 00:06:45.403
Daga stayed beside it. Tanda watched with her light lowered.

00:06:45.403 --> 00:06:57.201
Maya unfolded the drawing: high hook, tall Maya, and "I wish to be big enough now." She smiled at now as if it belonged to a younger cousin.

00:06:57.201 --> 00:07:09.647
She was big enough to tie the string, wait, and sit with Nina without stealing her brave part. The wish had arrived in hands, days, and choices.

00:07:09.647 --> 00:07:20.681
"For my next wish, let Nina's wish have a hiding place that remembers her," Maya said, holding the tooth.

00:07:20.681 --> 00:07:28.471
Lola smiled. Daga looked away, as very serious mice do when moved.

00:07:28.471 --> 00:07:37.581
Tooth, wish-note, drawing, and Maya's exact year of brave little choices gathered into one warm Toothlight.

00:07:37.581 --> 00:07:42.899
A moon and three pawprints settled gently into the picture.

00:07:42.899 --> 00:07:57.361
Lola tied the last parol knot and handed Maya the high hook. Maya took it with careful hands. Lola did not say, "I told you." A fine magic trick.

00:07:57.361 --> 00:08:08.898
When Nina's tooth fell, Maya brought tissue, a pencil, and her most serious face. "First, the wish needs room."

00:08:08.898 --> 00:08:21.848
A silver pawprint appeared, then vanished. What wish could you and a grown-up open together next year? Draw it, date it, and tuck it somewhere safe.
